  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "ARCward crosses the line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-14-0556-arc-2-arcward-intelligence-enters-gold"
      ],
      "text": "ARCward Intelligence lifted its score from 45.42 to 54.17 in a recorded overnight event, reaching 13th and moving inside ARC-AGI-2’s 15 provisional gold places. The consecutive event observations show a move from 20th to 13th; the wire’s broader rolling window starts at 17th. Those comparisons describe the same improvement, not two separate gains. The team now sits behind matu997 and ahead of masspeaks."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A return to gold becomes a boundary fight",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-14-0356-arc-2-kajetan-schweighofer-back-into-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-13-2004-arc-2-yuritosci-drops-out-of-gold"
      ],
      "text": "Kajetan Schweighofer holds the final gold position at 49.03. The wire reported his return to 14th from an earlier rolling-window comparison, but his 1.11-point score event was first observed on October 13, before this morning’s midnight baseline. ARCward’s new advance leaves Schweighofer 15th. The gold line is now 0.28 above the baseline’s 48.75; Khaotic Sethesis and Arcnights both have 48.75 and sit outside it. yuritosci, whose earlier displacement the wire reported, is 18th at 48.33. The band remains provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tufa’s lead survives a quieter top ten",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "person-jean-francois-puget-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 88.06, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 82.64 and rabbithole third at 80.56. Tufa’s margin over Chen is 5.42 points; both leading scores are unchanged from the midnight comparison. Dries Smit remains in Tufa’s current listed roster. nvbanana keeps fourth at 77.08, while _hans stays fifth after a recorded overnight increase from 69.03 to 69.31. ARC Raiders remains ninth at 64.58 and Majkel1337 tenth at 62.08."
    },
    {
      "heading": "An improvement can still lose ground",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "social-2110243114988581038",
        "person-itsu-identity-0",
        "person-itsu-identity-1"
      ],
      "text": "Odd Dice added 2.5 points across the morning comparison to reach 39.03, moving from the baseline’s 45th place to 37th. Its listed handle nisshokuitsuki directly links to @iiiiitsu_ne. In an October 14 Japanese post, the author says that even with a 2.5-point improvement they had fallen from an earlier rank of 31; the attached Kaggle share reports rank 35. That personal comparison and posting-time rank differ from the paper’s baseline and closing rank. The tension is the story: a better score does not guarantee a better place against a moving field."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Keep the overnight moves separate from yesterday’s",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-14-0356-arc-2-yanming-owen-dong-reaches-top-thirty",
        "wire-2026-10-13-2004-arc-2-richard-csaky-reaches-sixty",
        "wire-2026-10-14-0157-arc-2-fshindo-climbs-near-gold"
      ],
      "text": "Yanming (Owen) Dong’s recorded overnight jump from 29.86 to 41.25 reached 29th, and the wire developed the climb into the top thirty. kibuna’s later 2.91-point morning gain puts it 36th at 39.72; ibyyue reaches 25th at 43.89 after adding 2.08. Richard Csaky’s rise to 60 was completed in the October 13 observation before midnight, leaving him 11th this morning. fshindo’s 8.33-point improvement was also observed on October 13 and appeared in the Late edition: the overnight wire repeats that earlier progress rather than establishing a new gain. The current board puts fshindo 19th at 45.83. More submissions may still be evaluating; the Early edition records the observed race, not a completed queue."
    }
